course: dictionary
lesson: 3322
title: Evaporation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Evaporation is when a liquid, usually water, slowly turns into a gas called vapour and goes into the air. «Evaporation lifts water from seas, lakes and soil into the air.» The water has not vanished. It has changed into an invisible gas that floats up.
explain: The words around evaporation give clues. Lifts tells you the water moves upwards, and vapour is the gas it turns into. Evaporation can also mean something slowly disappearing, but in science it means the change from liquid to gas.
explain: Evaporation is faster when it is warm, windy, or the surface of the water is wide. «Evaporation leaves a dissolved solid behind.» When sea water dries out, the water leaves and the salt stays behind.
fact: Evaporation is a change of state, from liquid to gas.
fact: Evaporation happens at the surface of a liquid at any temperature, when the fastest particles escape as vapour.
fact: «Evaporation» is faster when it is warm, windy, or the surface is wide.
fact: Evaporation is part of the water cycle: evaporation, condensation (clouds), precipitation (rain), collection.
fact: «Evaporation cools what is left behind, because the fastest particles leave.» This is why sweating cools you down.
exercise: «Evaporation lifts water from seas, lakes and soil into the air.» What happens to the water here? | *It turns into a gas and goes into the air | Lake water sinks to the bottom and stays there | It turns into salt | It turns into solid ice
exercise: «Evaporation leaves a dissolved solid behind.» When sea water evaporates, what is left behind? | Rain | Vapour | Air | *Salt
exercise: «Evaporation cools what is left behind, because the fastest particles leave.» Which particles escape first? | The particles at the top of the cup only | The slowest particles | *The fastest particles | The heaviest particles
test: Which conditions make evaporation happen faster? | *Warm, windy weather and a wide surface | Freezing temperatures and no wind | Darkness and a closed lid | Cold, still air and a small surface
test: Which stage of the water cycle comes straight after evaporation? | Collection in the sea | Erosion of rock | *Condensation, when vapour forms clouds | Melting of snow
exam: Which word means the water vapour cooling and turning back into tiny droplets to form clouds? | *Condensation | Collection | Precipitation | Evaporation
